[[15,1,0,"<h3 class=\"step\" data-step=\"removing\" data-part=\"removal\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/20.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Removing</h3><a class=\"jump\" href=\"#\" data-jump=\"refitting\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/21.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Refitting</a><p>Position the vehicle on a lift\nand raise it.</p><p><a href=\"#/2429259\">4450B06</a></p><p>1. Undo the bolts.</p><p>2. Undo the plastic bolts.</p><p>3. Remove the wheel arch releasing it from its housing.</p><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2045267.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"],[15,1,0,"<h3 class=\"step\" data-step=\"refitting\" data-part=\"refit\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/21.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Refitting</h3><a class=\"jump\" href=\"#\" data-jump=\"removing\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/20.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Removing</a><p>Check that the wheelarch is\nundamaged.</p><p>Place the wheel arch in position and secure\nit using the bolts.</p><p><a href=\"#/2429259\">4450B06</a></p>"]]